---
// The deploying guide: Inngest Cloud and an app running in containers behind a load balancer, with what crosses
// between them and which keys each crossing uses.
import Figure from './Figure.astro';
---

<Figure>
  <div class="fig-flow" style="--cols: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(11rem, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr)">
    <div class="fig-node accent">
      <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 18h10a4 4 0 0 0 .6-7.95A6 6 0 0 0 6.2 9.2 4.4 4.4 0 0 0 7 18z"></path></svg>
      <p class="name">Inngest Cloud</p>
      <p class="detail">or a self-hosted Inngest</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fig-link">
      <div class="fig-arrow forward coral"><span>signed POST /api/inngest</span></div>
      <div class="fig-arrow back ok"><span>events, with the event key</span></div>
      <div class="fig-arrow back plan"><span>functions, on each sync</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fig-node">
      <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3 3 7.5l9 4.5 9-4.5zM3 12l9 4.5 9-4.5M3 16.5l9 4.5 9-4.5"></path></svg>
      <p class="name">Your app, in containers</p>
      <p class="detail">behind a load balancer at <code>https://shop.example.com</code>; any instance can answer</p>
      <ul class="extra fig-keys" aria-label="Environment of each container">
        <li>INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY</li>
        <li>INNGEST_EVENT_KEY</li>
        <li>INNGEST_SERVE_ORIGIN</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    In production, Inngest calls the app's public endpoint with requests signed by the signing key, and any instance
    behind the load balancer can answer them. The app sends events with the event key, and reports its functions to
    Inngest when it syncs after a deploy.
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
